\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Proved pointwise CAR-norm continuity of free dynamics and a sufficient uniform-in-time cutoff convergence criterion.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the full supplied definition, catalogue wording, source qualifications and listed references for 30006190. No fresh status or novelty search was performed. The argument below proves its auxiliary statements directly and does not import an unverified external theorem.

\paragraph{Unbounded free energy is not itself an obstruction.} Let \(U_t\) be a strongly continuous unitary group on a one-particle Hilbert space, possibly generated by an unbounded Hamiltonian. On the CAR algebra, the free automorphism is \(\tau_t(a(f))=a(U_tf)\). The CAR norm identity is \(\|a(g)\|=\|g\|\): the upper bound follows from \(a(g)^*a(g)+a(g)a(g)^*=\|g\|^2I\), and equality follows by acting on the normalized one-particle vector in direction \(g\). Consequently
\[
 \|\tau_t(a(f))-a(f)\|=\|(U_t-I)f\|\longrightarrow0.
\]
Telescoping products proves continuity on polynomials in the generators. Approximate any CAR element by such a polynomial and use isometry of automorphisms to extend norm continuity to the norm closure.
\paragraph{A sufficient cutoff passage criterion.} For interacting cutoff automorphisms \(\tau_t^\sigma\), suppose on a norm-dense subalgebra and some fixed \(T>0\), \(\sup_{|t|\leq T}\|\tau_t^\sigma(A)-\tau_t(A)\|\to0\). Then
\[
 \|\tau_t(A)-A\|\leq
 2\sup_{|s|\leq T}\|\tau_s^\sigma(A)-\tau_s(A)\|
 +\|\tau_t^\sigma(A)-A\|,
\]
where the factor two is a harmless upper bound. Fix a small cutoff error, then let \(t\to0\); density extends the result if the limit is an isometric automorphism group.
\paragraph{First interaction gap.} The source asks whether such a limiting many-body dynamics exists with sufficient norm control as Gaussian smearing is removed. Fixed-cutoff continuity and strong operator convergence in a representation do not supply the displayed uniform norm approximation. Proving that estimate, or a suitable equicontinuity substitute with algebra invariance, is the first missing step. The free calculation is a boundary check, not an answer for unregularized interactions.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked the CAR norm identity, extension from polynomials by isometry, order of the cutoff/time limits and distinction from strong operator continuity. Model self-audit only; no independent human mathematical verification. Applied contribution prompt A before drafting and B afterwards. Checked the CAR norm identity, extension from polynomials by isometry, order of the cutoff/time limits and distinction from strong operator continuity. First remaining gap: Establish norm approximation or equicontinuity and algebra invariance for the actual interacting ultraviolet cutoff limit. The inherited source status is preserved; original-target completion remains zero. Additional GPT-6 Astra reviewer (ultra reasoning): Checked the CAR norm identity using the anticommutator for the upper bound and a normalized one-particle Fock vector for the lower bound. Checked the free continuity calculation ||a(U\_t f)-a(f)||=||(U\_t-I)f|| and its extension through finite products and norm-dense polynomials using automorphism isometry. Checked the uniform-in-time cutoff convergence criterion: its displayed factor two is a valid loose upper bound, and the stated isometric-limit assumption is sufficient for the density extension. Confirmed the manuscript uses pointwise CAR operator-norm continuity, not strong operator topology, and does not claim existence/invariance of the unregularized interacting limit.

\paragraph{Tools, process and contributions.}
Python 3 and local file tools used to read definitions and serialize manuscripts. Calculations are symbolic reasoning; no numerical experiment or theorem prover. Contribution prompt A was followed by prompt B. GPT-6 Astra with ultra reasoning drafted the research and performed its stated self-audit; any additional coordinator contribution is identified in the verification and audit. A GPT-6-based Codex coordinator assembled the manuscript and checked repository integration; its exact variant and reasoning configuration were not exposed. No human mathematical contribution, independent human proof check or formal proof certification is supplied. Complete derivations and the consulted source references are included here; private reasoning transcripts are not published.

\paragraph{Final status and first remaining gap.}
